From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vadim Kochan <vadim4j@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 06:20:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] KVM: arm64: initialize EL2 heap during pKVM setup

The Android pKVM device-assignment implementation adds a dynamically
refillable EL2 heap and uses it for IOMMU domain-private data.  The 7.1
port included the allocator implementation but omitted the donor's setup
call, leaving its list head and lock zero-initialized.

A translated host DMA domain reaches hyp_alloc() while the pKVM IOMMU
driver is initialized.  It then treats the zero list head as a populated
list and dereferences address zero, causing an nVHE panic.

Initialize the 128 MiB private virtual-address range during __pkvm_init(),
matching the Android 6.18 donor.  This runs after the final hyp mappings are
created and before host IOMMU drivers can allocate EL2 domains.

Signed-off-by: Vadim Kochan <vadim4j@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/setup.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/setup.c b/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/setup.c
index 9e4be27b8..5444334f9 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/setup.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/setup.c
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 #include <asm/kvm_pgtable.h>
 #include <asm/kvm_pkvm.h>
 
+#include <nvhe/alloc.h>
 #include <nvhe/early_alloc.h>
 #include <nvhe/ffa.h>
 #include <nvhe/gfp.h>
@@ -382,6 +383,10 @@ int __pkvm_init(phys_addr_t phys, unsigned long size, unsigned long *per_cpu_bas
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	ret = hyp_alloc_init(SZ_128M);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
 	update_nvhe_init_params();
 
 	/* Jump in the idmap page to switch to the new page-tables */
-- 
